{"name":"Poached Rainbow Trout","hex":"#ff8552","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poached","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of poach"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by poaching.","Obtained by poaching."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poached"},{"term":"rainbow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A multicoloured arch in the sky, produced by prismatic refraction of light within droplets of rain in the air.","Any prismatic refraction of light showing a spectrum of colours."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Multicolored, especially if in rainbow order.","Made up of several races or ethnicities, or (more broadly) of several cultural or ideological factions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainbow"},{"term":"trout","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of fish in Salmonidae, closely related to salmon, and distinguished by spawning more than once.","An objectionable elderly woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for trout.","To (figuratively) slap someone with a slimy, stinky, wet trout; to admonish jocularly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trout"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rainbow trout","blocks":[{"text":"The rainbow trout is a species of trout native to cold-water tributaries of the Pacific Ocean in North America and Asia. The steelhead is an anadromous (sea-run) form of the coastal rainbow trout (O. m. irideus) or Columbia River redband trout (O. m. gairdneri) that usually returns to freshwater to spawn after living two to three years in the ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Close_up_of_rainbow_trout_fish_underwater_oncorhynchus_mykiss.jpg/330px-Close_up_of_rainbow_trout_fish_underwater_oncorhynchus_mykiss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_trout","wikidata":"Q187986"},{"title":"Rainbow","blocks":[{"text":"A rainbow is an optical phenomenon caused by refraction, internal reflection and dispersion of light in water droplets resulting in a continuous spectrum of light appearing in the sky. The rainbow takes the form of a multicoloured circular arc. Rainbows caused by sunlight always appear in the section of sky directly opposite the sun. Rainbows can be caused by many forms of airborne water. These include not only rain, but also mist, spray, and airborne dew."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg/330px-Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow","wikidata":"Q1052"},{"title":"Trout","blocks":[{"text":"Trout is a generic common name for numerous species of carnivorous freshwater fishes belonging to the genera Oncorhynchus, Salmo, and Salvelinus, all of which are members of the subfamily Salmoninae in the family Salmonidae. The word trout is also used for some similar-shaped but non-salmonid fish, such as the spotted seatrout/speckled trout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Salmo_trutta.jpg/330px-Salmo_trutta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trout","wikidata":"Q2258881"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Oncorhynchus_mykiss_ssp._gairdneri.jpg/500px-Oncorhynchus_mykiss_ssp._gairdneri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Oncorhynchus_mykiss_ssp._gairdneri.jpg/500px-Oncorhynchus_mykiss_ssp._gairdneri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOncorhynchus_mykiss_ssp._gairdneri.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi